  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R13 and R15 establish that accurate, computationally efficient MTPs can be trained on DFT data for the closely related BCC MoNbTaW refractory alloy, while R11 supplies direct evidence that SRO is an energetically consequential structural mediator in that system. R5 also connects atomistic potentials, DFT validation, and SRO in a refractory HEA, and several magnetic/free-energy records show generally that small finite-temperature electronic or entropic contributions can shift phase stability. However, none of the records proposes liquid-phase MTP sampling coupled to free-energy perturbation, identifies small MTP–DFT energy-difference variance as the basis for rapid FEP convergence, or replaces thermodynamic integration with FEP. They also do not connect a Fermi-level DOS gap and SRO stabilization quantitatively to melting-temperature shifts. Thus the literature points toward an MTP-based treatment and relevant free-energy corrections, but the combined MTP–FEP melting methodology requires a substantial additional idea."
